{
  "_note": "How each region and province plays (src/provinceRules.ts, docs/ONLINE_PLAN.md 5.2). Each layer lists only what it changes: the game's defaults, then the region's, then the province's. Multipliers are 0.1-5 (1 = as the game is), months are 1-12, chancePerMonth is 0-1, drought.share (how much less a water works gives in a dry-season month, when only rain or a storm fills the ground, a little) is 0-0.9. weather (src/weather.ts) lists twelve numbers 0-1 for each month, January first: rain, the chance the month is wet; storm, the share of wet months that are storms (heavy rain); fog, the share of dry months that are foggy; smoke, the haze of burning fields and forests; and flood, the chance a storm month floods low land beside the water (only while disasters are on). festivals (src/festivals.ts) adds a region's or province's festivals to the country's own (New Year, Songkran, Loy Krathong), by id, each with its month 1-12 and any of its numbers to change (draw, homecoming, waterUse, and pairs for modest and grand: cost, land, fire, rubbish, dirt; cheer has not held, modest, grand); null takes one away. farmZone (src/farmZone.ts, src/farmCrops.ts, docs/GAME_DESIGN.md section 7) changes any of the farm zone's numbers (price a tile, reach in tiles, eraTop, feeds, exportPerLevel, the land's choice of kind, dryYield, dryDraw, hubReach, hubBonus, landValue, visitors, haze, factoriesPerLevel), under kinds any of a paddy's, field's, orchard's or pond's (sale, jobs, draw, chemicals, burns, mud, ground), and under crops any of the eighteen crops' numbers (kind, weight 0-1 where 0 means not grown there, and [min, max] pairs for rise, slope, ground, water, town; section 7.6). Edited by the owner; once the game is online the same data lives in the server's database and an admin page edits it.",
